Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Offset: a removed face met only tangentially is closed by wall strips along
the normal (mitcad#2462).

A removed face (a cap) whose edges each bound a kept face tangent to it
there whose offset does not vanish (a top with all its edges rounded,
shelled with the top open by a wall no thicker than the rounding; GitHub
#645's loft, 2 mm with 2 mm roundings): the kept faces' offsets run under
the cap, parallel to it at its edges, and never meet it. The thick solid
intersected the cap all the same, found no section, and failed (the
intersection join) or came out invalid (the arc join).

Such a cap is now no cap: MakeOffsetShape takes it out of the caps and of
the images SetFaces gave it, its edges are free edges of the offset, and
after the faces are built MakeMissingWalls, restricted to those edges,
builds the strip from each edge to its offset, which MakeThickSolid glues
in; Clear empties the walls. In the intersection join the offsets of two
roundings mitred at a corner touch at the offset of the corner's vertex on
the cap, and the intersection of their enlarged offsets is two curves
crossing there, all kept: Inter3D now cuts it there
(DropBranchesAtTangentEnd), keeping of the pieces at that point only the
one going back along the edge.

Not covered: a wall as thick as a circular rounding (its offset vanishes,
and the face beyond meets the cap on the cap's edge), and a rounding of
more than four edges beside a cap where the wall is thicker than it
(FindVanishingFaces takes four-edged faces only): see the topic doc.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2462.

